{"parentUuid":"78f09d10-6850-4b08-ba30-c5529264cfcc","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/harborlight","sessionId":"insight-21","version":"2.0.21","gitBranch":"fix/publish-dist","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01X4fPxuxEnGQnfNudU9LJcZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That's the cause. PR 521 deleted .npmignore as an unused config file. It was not unused: with it gone, npm falls back to .gitignore, which lists dist/ because the build output is not committed. So npm publish left out the compiled code and shipped the TypeScript sources instead. package.json has no files field, which would have prevented this.\n\nThe robust fix is a files field in package.json: it lists what goes into the package and takes precedence over the ignore files, so the build output is included even though git ignores it, and src/ stays out without a .npmignore."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":410,"output_tokens":574}},"uuid":"5a02a883-2735-4788-8f5a-728a716eef86","timestamp":"2026-10-06T10:03:59.000Z","requestId":"req_011CHBWt4L6vRgwC1RS9kt10"}
